an&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-meta"&gt;2023–Present&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;p class="entry-sub"&gt;University of Vienna&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry-head"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-title"&gt;Master of Science, Communication Science&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-meta"&gt;2020–2022&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;p class="entry-sub"&gt;University of Vienna&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry-head"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-title"&gt;Bachelor of Arts, Political Science&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-meta"&gt;2018&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;p class="entry-sub"&gt;The University of Queensland&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry-head"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-title"&gt;Bachelor of Journalism&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-meta"&gt;2018&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;p class="entry-sub"&gt;The University of Queensland&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/section&gt;&#10;&lt;section class="grid-section"&gt;&#10; &lt;h2 class="grid-label"&gt;Teaching &amp;amp; Service&lt;/h2&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="grid-content"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry-head"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-title"&gt;Lecturer, Department of Communication&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-meta"&gt;2025–Present&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;p class="entry-sub"&gt;University of Vienna&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry-head"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-title"&gt;Local Organizing Committee, COMPTEXT&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-meta"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;p class="entry-sub"&gt;University of Vienna&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/section&gt;</description></item><item><title>Research</title><link>https://sebs.md/research/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>sebastian.edward.sherrah@univie.ac.at (Sebastian Sherrah)</author><guid>https://sebs.md/research/</guid><description>&lt;section class="grid-section"&gt;&#10; &lt;h2 class="grid-label"&gt;Working Papers&lt;/h2&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="grid-content"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry-head"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-title"&gt;When, Where, and for Whom Media Exposure Matters: A Comparative Reassessment of Media Effects on Vote Choice&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-meta"&gt;2026&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;p class="entry-sub"&gt;With Jakob-Moritz Eberl, Petro Tolochko &amp;amp; Hajo G. Boomgaarden · Presented at ICA 2026, Cape Town&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;p class="entry-note"&gt;Uses Bayesian multilevel out-of-sample predictive modelling across 70 elections in 46 countries (CSES) to test when reported political media exposure adds predictive information about vote choice beyond political predispositions.&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="entry-head"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-title"&gt;&lt;a href="https://ecpr.eu/Events/Event/PaperDetails/80906" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Too Much Alarmism? Experimental Insights into Misinformation Communication&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="entry-meta"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;p class="entry-sub"&gt;With Jakob-Moritz Eberl, Marie Heřmanová &amp;amp; Matouš Pilnáček&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;p class="entry-note"&gt;Preregistered survey experiment in Austria and the Czech Republic testing how alarmist, balanced, and reassuring frames about misinformation shape democratic perceptions, trust, and counter-speech.&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/section&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>